  "text": "Recipe: Lentil Waffles\nCreator: Vandana Gupta\nCategory: Waffles\nIngredients: yellow split lentils, red lentils, barnyard millet powder, onion, ginger, green chillies, cumin seeds, hing (asafoetida), turmeric powder, red chilli powder, ajwain (carom seeds), salt, water\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, bake\nInstructions: BATTER: Soak yellow & red lentils for an hour. Grind them into a fine paste with only 1/2 cup water for thick consistency like pancake or waffle batter. Add the remaining ingredients. Mix well. WAFFLES: Pour batter into a waffle maker. Cook for 10 mins \u2014 adjust heat settings in waffle maker per your needs.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (barnyard millet powder), BEANS (red lentils, yellow split lentils), RAINBOW VEGGIES (onion), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
